The SQL queries in this directory are TPC-H benchmark queries augmented with a
vector-search range predicate over synthetic embedding columns ("TPC-H+V").

--- TPC-H ---

TPC-H is a decision support benchmark developed and maintained by the Transaction
Processing Performance Council (TPC). The benchmark specification and queries are
Copyright (C) 1993-2022 Transaction Processing Performance Council. All rights reserved.

These queries are used here solely for non-commercial benchmarking and research purposes
in accordance with the TPC Fair Use Policy (https://www.tpc.org/tpc_documents_current_versions/pdf/tpc_fair_use_policy.pdf).

The source of the benchmark specification is: https://www.tpc.org/tpch/

--- Vector augmentation (TPC-H+V) ---

The idea of augmenting TPC-H with embedding columns and vector-search predicates
is drawn from:

    Exqutor: Extended Query Optimizer for Vector-augmented Analytical Queries.
    arXiv:2512.09695. https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.09695

("TPC-H+V" above is our informal nickname for this augmented dataset, not the
paper's benchmark name.)

The SQL in this directory is authored independently from the public TPC-H
specification (https://www.tpc.org/tpch/); it is NOT copied from the Exqutor
paper's accompanying repository, which is licensed CC BY-NC 4.0. Only the
augmentation scheme (which tables carry embeddings, and the shape of the
pgvector range predicate) is taken from the paper. The embedding columns
(part.p_text_embedding, partsupp.ps_image_embedding, partsupp.ps_text_embedding,
partsupp.ps_tag) are generated deterministically by testdata/generate_testdata.sh.
